 on the unit circle, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})=-1.\n$$\n\nHowever, $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ does not lie within the range of $\\theta .$ To get an angle that's coterminal with $\\frac{3\\pi }{2}$ that lies within the range of $\\theta ,$ we subtract $2\\pi .$\n\n$$\n\\frac{3\\pi }{2}-2\\pi =-\\frac{\\pi }{2}\n$$\n\nHence,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡(-1)=-\\frac{\\pi }{2}.\n$$" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427519 1080 "18" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427519 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427519 1083 #uuid "0e3ea772-e772-52b8-9654-53b9a628393a" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427520 1080 "{90}^{∘}" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427520 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427520 1083 #uuid "108019a0-46c5-5872-8b39-0d3a33f620c2" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427521 1080 "-\\pi " 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427521 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427521 1083 #uuid "362fffeb-2576-5d58-b4ac-2e8e14f21e76" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427522 1080 "{30}^{∘}" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427522 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427522 1083 #uuid "5234a80f-3964-5f6b-929f-0367338cb2a2" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427523 1080 "\\frac{3\\pi }{2}" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427523 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427523 1083 #uuid "722eb547-e288-5ad4-ab49-790d9559959d" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427524 1080 "{45}^{∘}" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427524 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427524 1083 #uuid "9f118ded-6d77-5044-83fb-ddb49902a5ca" 13194139534606 17592186045417 true] [17592186427525 1080 "{60}^{∘}" 13194139534606